WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.500
The first cybertruck built with 4680 cells from Tesla's Gulf Coast refinery shows internal battery

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:14.140
supply scaling in Texas. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 595. Tesla produced its initial

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:20.600
cybertruck using 4680 cells that incorporate lithium-refined at the company's Gulf Coast facility

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:26.880
in Robstown, Texas. This marks visible progress on the structural battery pack and cell production

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:32.980
targets at gigatexas. The development ties directly into ongoing efforts to raise energy density

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:39.100
and lower cell costs for high volume models. The refinery supplies the raw lithium that enters

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:44.140
the cell manufacturing line before the completed packs reach the cybertruck assembly line.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:49.800
Next milestone to watch is whether the same cell chemistry appears in additional vehicle lines

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:55.540
beyond the cybertruck. Production scaling at gigatexas continues to build on earlier structural

00:00:55.540 --> 00:01:01.140
pack shipments in select vehicles. The next step will show whether this chemistry moves into other

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:09.780
lines. Tesla confirmed FSD supervised version 14.3.9 will begin rolling out soon. It introduces

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:15.760
automatic collision evasion, which can take steering, braking, and acceleration control when frontal

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:21.720
collision risk exceeds what emergency braking alone can handle. The feature activates under specific

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:27.920
conditions such as divided roads and speeds under 85 miles per hour. It can also intervene on

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:34.120
severe driver inattention. Employees are already testing the build internally before wider early access

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:40.080
distribution. The system steers into another lane or onto the shoulder if needed while the driver

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:45.720
cannot cancel the maneuver by pressing the accelerator. Only strong counter steering force ends the

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:52.260
intervention once it begins. Lemonade introduced simultaneous car and autonomous car policies in Missouri

00:01:52.260 --> 00:02:00.520
that grant Tesla drivers an immediate 50% discount per mile when using FSD supervised. Company President

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:06.720
Shai Wininger stated the pricing models recognize lower accident risk from the data and pass savings

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:13.440
directly to customers. The move gives FSD users a concrete insurance benefit in one state while

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:19.180
lemonade tests the approach as a first for its platform. Missouri drivers receive both products at

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:24.900
launch, which the insurer described as a first for its own rollout sequence. The discount applies

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:32.020
instantly once FSD supervised is engaged on eligible trips. Insurance pricing for supervised driver

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:39.200
assistance systems rests on a narrow data window. Lemonade's Missouri offering applies a 50% per mile

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:45.300
discount based on observed accident reduction in FSD data, yet that reduction is measured only

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:51.280
while a human remains legally responsible. The arrangement works because current liability still sits

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:57.060
with the driver, allowing the insurer to treat the software as a risk mitigator rather than the primary

00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:03.300
operator. Missouri therefore functions as a controlled experiment where the discount reflects correlation

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:09.760
rather than causation of full autonomy. If unsupervised operation arrives, that liability

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:15.420
assignment changes. The same discount logic would then require the vehicle manufacturer or fleet

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:21.140
operator to carry the risk directly, shifting the economics from per mile savings for owners

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:27.360
to per mile costs for the company providing the ride. Tesla received city approval to develop a

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:33.160
robot taxi facility near the San Antonio Airport. The site adds to the growing list of operational

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:39.400
locations beyond the initial Austin deployment. Local permitting progress provides one concrete data

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:45.320
point on how quickly additional markets can come online once vehicles are in service. The approval

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:51.080
covers infrastructure needed to support fleet operations in the area. No timeline for construction

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:58.240
start or vehicle numbers was released with the decision. NHTSA opened an audit into Tesla's self-certification

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:04.640
of the cyber cab after commercial rides began in Austin. The agency is examining the technical data

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:11.120
Tesla used to declare the vehicle compliant with all applicable FMVSS despite the lack of conventional

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:16.820
controls. The review will assess whether certain standards were deemed inapplicable and how that

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:22.440
determination was reached. Tesla notified the agency that it plans to expand the small initial

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:28.460
fleet gradually which triggered the formal query process. The outcome will influence how quickly

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:34.560
additional cities can receive similar deployments. Tesla introduced a rare earth-free motor design

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:41.480
that reduces reliance on specific mined materials. The change addresses supply chain concentration risks

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:47.600
without delivering the dramatic cost or performance leap some coverage implied. It still requires

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:52.860
careful engineering trade-offs on torque and efficiency that will be tested in production vehicles.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:59.640
The motor targets the same power output range as prior designs while eliminating neodymium and other

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:05.260
rare earth elements. Production validation will determine whether the material substitution scales

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:12.800
without added weight or complexity. The IIHS awarded both the key ateluride and Tesla Model Y,

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:19.240
its top safety pick plus rating in the latest round of evaluations. The Model Y achieved the

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:25.660
distinction alongside a conventional 3-row SUV in a segment where several premium sedans fell short.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:31.420
The result adds another data point on how Tesla's structural and sensor package performs in

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:37.120
standardized crash tests. The award covers both frontal and side impact performance plus

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:42.460
roof strength and headlight ratings. Model Y joins a short list of vehicles that met the

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:50.440
stricter 2024 IIHS criteria across all tested categories. Owners shared practical advice for using

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:56.600
the new CyberCab service in Austin. Riders noted that the absence of manual controls changes how

00:05:56.600 --> 00:06:01.780
passengers interact with the vehicle during the ride. Several users compared the experience to

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:07.380
early ride chair apps but with lower visible driver oversight. The tips thread highlights small

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:13.440
operational details that only surface once paid rides begin. One recurring note concerned how to

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:19.240
request stops or adjust climate settings through the passenger interface alone. The discussion also

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:24.140
covered etiquette around entering and exiting without a driver present to confirm the destination.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:30.660
A Deutsche Bank tracker indicated neo-orders outpacing Tesla in parts of the Chinese market during

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:36.360
a recent period. The comparison arrives as both companies prepare broader model refreshes.

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:42.220
It offers one snapshot of competitive intensity in Tesla's largest single-country sales region.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:48.260
The tracker focuses on order intake rather than final deliveries, providing an earlier signal

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:53.420
than monthly sales reports. Tesla has maintained a strong position in premium segments,

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:59.300
yet the data shows neo-gaining ground in volume-oriented categories. The ad drew attention

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:04.120
for showcasing the vehicle without addressing certain regulatory or operational constraints.

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:09.520
Commenters focused on the gap between the polished marketing and the current limited deployment

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:15.540
scope. The reaction shows how public perception can shift quickly when visuals outpace real-world

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:21.780
availability. The campaign highlighted interior space and ride comfort while omitting details on

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:28.620
route restrictions and supervision requirements. Observers noted the ad ran widely before the NHTSA

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:36.620
audit query became public. Now, one thing worth watching is the NHTSA audit into cybercab self-certification.

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:42.280
The agency is reviewing how Tesla declared the vehicle compliant without conventional controls.

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:49.820
The review focuses on which FMVSS standards were deemed inapplicable. Tesla notified the agency of

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:55.960
plans to expand the initial fleet gradually. The audit adds a layer of regulatory scrutiny at a time

00:07:55.960 --> 00:08:01.980
when fleet expansion plans are still forming. Before we go, watch for any updates on how the rare

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:07.320
earth-free motor performs in early validation testing. That's your Tesla news for today.

